// Gateway B (service `openclaw-cto`): CTO exposed over A2A, reads the repo mounted at target/.
//   docker compose exec openclaw-cto openclaw config patch --file /project/config/homework-cto.patch.json5
{
  channels: {
    a2a: {
      enabled: true,
      exposeAgents: ["cto"],
      replyTimeoutMs: 600000,
      peers: { main: { token: "${A2A_CTO_TOKEN}" } },
    },
    // Telegram belongs to gateway A; both polling one bot token conflict.
    telegram: { enabled: false },
  },
  bindings: [{ agentId: "cto", match: { channel: "a2a" } }],
  gateway: { controlUi: { allowedOrigins: ["http://127.0.0.1:18791", "http://localhost:18791"] } },
  plugins: { entries: { "diagnostics-otel": { enabled: true } } },
  diagnostics: {
    enabled: true,
    otel: {
      enabled: true,
      tracesEndpoint: "http://phoenix:6006/v1/traces",
      protocol: "http/protobuf",
      serviceName: "openclaw-cto",
      traces: true,
      metrics: false,
      logs: false,
      captureContent: true,
    },
  },
  // CTO answers alone here: no delegation, no MCP.
  agents: { entries: { cto: { tools: { deny: ["sessions_spawn", "subagents"] } } } },
}
